{{!-- Recommendations: the publications this one reads.

A Directory in the CONTEXT.md sense — it lists something other than posts — but the only one whose
rows are neither tags nor authors, and the only one a `{{#get}}` cannot fetch. The list is drawn by
partials/recommendations.hbs, which the `{{recommendations}}` helper resolves by name; the layout
picker is read there rather than here, for the reason that file records.

`limit="100"` because the helper's own default is **5** (`parseOptions` in
core/frontend/helpers/recommendations.js), which would quietly truncate any publication that
recommends more than five — the same number Portal asks for.

THE GUARD IS NOT REDUNDANT. `{{recommendations}}` returns nothing at all when the feature is off,
so without `{{#if @site.recommendations_enabled}}` the heading and the section's padding would
render around an empty page. Do not "simplify" it away. `{{#if}}`, not `{{#match}}` —
`{{#match}}` is a comparison helper. --}}
{{#post}}
	{{> "page-intro" eyebrow=(t "What we read") headingId="rec-title" padding="pt-16 pb-14" measure="max-w-[60ch]"}}

	{{#if @site.recommendations_enabled}}
		{{recommendations limit="100"}}
	{{else}}
		<section class="container pt-14">
			<p class="font-body text-muted">{{t "Recommendations are turned off for this publication."}}</p>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{> "newsletter" anchor="recs-newsletter" pt="pt-20"}}
{{/post}}
